## Self-exclusion statement

**Zero verified public benchmark numbers** found for Space Bunny Alpha / `space-bunny-free`.

The model is an anonymous stealth preview with an undisclosed vendor, available only as a free tier on OpenCode Zen. No Artificial Analysis model page (403), no BenchLM entry (404), no HuggingFace model card, no published benchmark scores, and no official model card or launch post with benchmark numbers could be located.

Per `RULES.md` §[Self-exclusion]: "if you found ZERO verified public benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID → refuse to score, write `Laguna_S_2.1.md.excluded` instead, and stop — do not fabricate or guess."

This model is therefore **self-excluded** from scoring. When Space Bunny Alpha is no longer anonymous (vendor disclosed) or publishes benchmark numbers on a public source (Artificial Analysis, BenchLM, HuggingFace, or an official announcement), this file should be replaced with a scored `Laguna_S_2.1.md`.

The model's `average.md` scores (Overall: 75.7) are derived from peer model ratings, not from verified public benchmarks. These peer ratings are internal cross-model assessments and do not constitute verified public benchmark numbers per the research methodology.

